    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="23">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 23</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">and ymbrenfæstena, swa swa s<hi rend="italic">anctu</hi>s Gregorius Angelcynne silf gedihte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="23" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ ymbren fæstena swa swa sanctus Gregorius Angelcynne sylf hit gedihte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And ymbrenfæstena, swa swa sanctus Gregorius Angelcynne sylf hit gedihte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And the fasts of the Ember Days [shall be observed] as St Gregory himself prescribed for the English nation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And the Ember Fasts are to be kept, just as Saint Gregory himself ordained for the English.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">und Quatemberfasten so, wie der heilige Gregor selbst der Englischen Nation es vorgeschrieben hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and the Ember fasts, as St Gregory himself prescribed it for the English nation.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:ICn_16">I Cn 16</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="450"><ref target="clause:VAtr_15">V Atr 15</ref></note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Ember Fasts: See note to 5 Æthelred 18.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
